window.LB_DESC_ADD({"grimoires/arclords-codex":"<p>The techniques bound in the spellbooks of the Arclords of Nex are jealously guarded secrets, and an Arclord gives up their grimoire only under the direst of circumstances. These grimoires vary in appearance based on their owner's taste, but all display the Arclords' symbol of an eye within a triangle on the cover. Possession of an Arclord's codex signifies mastery of powerful magic, and anyone who steals such a tome is sure to find themself hunted across the world—or the multiverse, if necessary—by its owner.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate—Third Eye Rejuvenation</strong> ◇ (concentrate, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared 10th-rank arcane spell, the magical energies reinvigorate your spellcasting. You regain access to two spells of 4th rank or lower or one spell of 5th rank or higher that you've prepared and already cast today.</p>","grimoires/bloodstained-treatise":"<p>The white leather cover of this book is splotched with rusty red bloodstains, and its pages seep red when turned, although this never stains the bearer's hands or clothing. Anatomical drawings illustrate its pages.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Sanguine Expulsion</strong> ◆ (concentrate, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell that manipulates blood, such as blood vendetta or vampiric exsanguination, or a spell dealing piercing or slashing damage, all targets of the triggering spell take 1d6 persistent bleed damage; if the spell already causes bleed damage, the bleed damage increases by 1d6. The wounds of one affected target (chosen by you) gush uncontrollably, covering the ground with blood in a 5-foot emanation that lasts for 1 round. Creatures that begin their turn in the blood must succeed at a Reflex save against your spell DC or fall Prone.</p>","grimoires/book-of-endless-walls":"<p>A circular labyrinth is etched onto this tome's cover, its lines shimmering silver. Touching the book causes a sense of faint discombobulation.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Bewildering Walls</strong> ◇ (concentrate, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared wall spell, such as Wall of Fire or Wall of Thorns, you imbue the wall with an uncanny sense of disorientation, causing creatures to perceive it as an endless labyrinth. Any creature that begins its turn within the wall's spaces or passes through the wall's spaces must attempt a Will save against your spell DC, in addition to the wall's normal effect. Regardless of the results, the target then becomes immune to Bewildering Walls for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The wall has no additional effect for that creature.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is bewildered by its perceptions of labyrinthine walls and treats all other creatures as Concealed for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature treats all other creatures as hidden for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature treats all other creatures as hidden for 1 round and concealed for 1 minute.</p>","grimoires/calligraphic-illumination":"<p>An ever-shifting series of calligraphic runes scrawls across the pages of this leather-bound book, as if written by an unseen hand. Calligraphic illuminations are sacred to the faith of Irez, Lady of Inscribed Wonder.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Inscribed Insight</strong> ◇ (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your last action was to Cast a prepared Spell that creates or manipulates written text or runes, such as Runic Body, the writing briefly forms into words conveying valuable information. Attempt to Recall Knowledge about any one creature or object that you can see with a +2 item bonus to the check.</p>","grimoires/chapbook-of-terrors-greater":"<p>This lurid pamphlet contains spooky tales about ghosts, monsters, and murderers, all illustrated in gruesome detail. The stories, fortunately, are only fictions… or are they?</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Horrify</strong> ◆ (concentrate, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the fear trait, creatures frightened by the spell also take 2d6 persistent mental damage as they dwell on your terrifying tale.</p>","grimoires/chapbook-of-terrors-major":"<p>This lurid pamphlet contains spooky tales about ghosts, monsters, and murderers, all illustrated in gruesome detail. The stories, fortunately, are only fictions… or are they?</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Horrify</strong> ◆ (concentrate, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the fear trait, creatures frightened by the spell also take 4d6 persistent mental damage as they dwell on your terrifying tale.</p>","grimoires/chapbook-of-terrors":"<p>This lurid pamphlet contains spooky tales about ghosts, monsters, and murderers, all illustrated in gruesome detail. The stories, fortunately, are only fictions… or are they?</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Horrify</strong> ◆ (concentrate, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the fear trait, creatures frightened by the spell also take 1d6 persistent mental damage as they dwell on your terrifying tale.</p>","grimoires/grudge-journal":"<p>The margins of this clothbound journal's pages are filled with complaints on all manner of topics, shifting to match whatever angers the bearer most.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Air Grievance</strong> ◆ (concentrate, curse, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You inscribe the name or description of a creature you can see that has wronged you in some way. If your next action is to target that creature with a prepared spell with the curse trait that requires a saving throw, the creature also becomes Drained 2 unless it critically succeeds its saving throw.</p>","grimoires/psalter-of-the-blessed":"<p>These gold-leafed volumes bear the religious symbol of a deity who allows or requires holy sanctification. Unholy creatures are Drained 2 as long as they keep the tome in their possession and can't recover from this condition.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Righteous Prayers</strong> ◆ (concentrate, holy, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the holy trait, the energy blesses you and your allies with celestial power. You and all allies within 30 feet of you gain fast healing 5 and a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws against effects from creatures with the unholy trait for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>Effect: Psalter of the Blessed</p>","grimoires/radiant-tome":"<p>A flawless diamond embedded into the cover of this tome gleams with an inner light, refracting multicolored rays to the eyes of viewers.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Flare</strong> ◆ (concentrate, light, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the light trait, the luminescence of the book grows even more intense, emitting bright light in a 15-foot emanation for 1 minute. Enemies that start their turn in this bright light must attempt a Fortitude save against your spell DC.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune to this bright light for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Blinded until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is blinded until the start of your next turn and Dazzled for 1 minute.</p>","grimoires/sparking-grimoire-greater":"<p>The black leather cover of this spellbook is embossed with a pattern of lightning, and sparks crackle across it. Touching the book makes one's hair stand slightly on end.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Static Shock</strong> ◇ (concentrate, electricity, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the electricity trait, you charge yourself with electrical energy. Until the end of your next turn, you and your allies' Strikes deal an additional 2d6 electricity damage, and creatures targeting you with a melee Strike or spell with a range of touch take 2d6 electricity damage, with a basic Reflex save against your spell DC.</p>","grimoires/sparking-grimoire":"<p>The black leather cover of this spellbook is embossed with a pattern of lightning, and sparks crackle across it. Touching the book makes one's hair stand slightly on end.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Static Shock</strong> ◇ (concentrate, electricity, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the electricity trait, you charge yourself with electrical energy. Until the end of your next turn, your Strikes deal an additional 2d6 electricity damage, and creatures targeting you with a melee Strike or spell with a range of touch take 2d6 electricity damage, with a basic Reflex save against your spell DC.</p>","grimoires/verdant-leaves-greater":"<p>The pages of this book are dried leaves in all colors of the seasons, their delicate veins spelling out incantations. It carries the earthy scent of a forest floor.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Nature's Resilience</strong> ◆ (concentrate, plant, wood)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your last action was to Cast a prepared Spell with the plant or wood trait, you imbue yourself with the strength of the natural world and obtain the effect of a 4th-rank Oaken Resilience spell.</p>","grimoires/verdant-leaves-major":"<p>The pages of this book are dried leaves in all colors of the seasons, their delicate veins spelling out incantations. It carries the earthy scent of a forest floor.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Nature's Resilience</strong> ◆ (concentrate, plant, wood)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your last action was to Cast a prepared Spell with the plant or wood trait, you imbue yourself with the strength of the natural world and obtain the effect of a 6th-rank Oaken Resilience spell.</p>","grimoires/verdant-leaves":"<p>The pages of this book are dried leaves in all colors of the seasons, their delicate veins spelling out incantations. It carries the earthy scent of a forest floor.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Nature's Resilience</strong> ◆ (concentrate, plant, wood)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your last action was to Cast a prepared Spell with the plant or wood trait, you imbue yourself with the strength of the natural world and obtain the effect of a 2nd-rank Oaken Resilience spell.</p>","grimoires/whispering-spirit-tome":"<p>Mystical incantations to commune with spirits are engraved on the flexible metal pages of this slender volume, and its gleaming silver cover ripples when touched.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Sense Phantasm</strong> ◆ (concentrate, detection, mental, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a prepared Spell with the spirit trait, you attune yourself to the spirit world, granting you greater insight into such phenomena. You gain the effects of Spirit Sense for 1 hour.</p>","contracts/accursed-fame":"<p>Infernal tongues spread word of your great deeds. Creatures that would have an initial attitude toward you other than hostile have their attitude improved by one step. Once per day, from any distance, the devil who holds your bargained contract can cite a defamation clause, rendering you unable to speak for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Entreat Crowd</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, emotion, magical, manipulate, mental, subtle)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You invoke a due diligence stipulation in your contract. Attempt a Diplomacy check to make a Request of the creature with the highest Will DC within 100 feet who isn't your ally; the GM might have you make a Request of the most influential creature instead. The result applies to all creatures within 100 feet that can understand you.</p>","contracts/exploitative-wealth":"<p>Hard work can earn some money, but truly grandiose wealth is built on the backs of others. Devils convince others to work for you, extracting value from them. You can Earn Income at the same time as you perform another downtime activity. Once per week, from any distance, the devil who holds your bargained contract can invoke a non-compete clause, imposing a –4 circumstance penalty to your checks to Earn Income for 1 week.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Enforce Competition</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You call upon an antitrust provision in your contract. The contract casts paranoia (DC 19), and if the target has more allies within the spell's range than you, they take a –2 circumstance penalty to their Will save.</p>","contracts/illicit-knowledge":"<p>Devils have learned much in their eternal lives, and you have access to some of their secrets. You gain the Additional Lore feat for Devil Lore, and during your daily preparations, you become trained in two Lore skills of your choice. Since these effects are temporary, you can't use them as prerequisites. Once per day, from any distance, the devil who holds your bargained contract can invoke an evidence concealment clause as a single action with the concentrate trait, leaving you Stupefied 2 for 1 hour; you can't reduce the value of this condition by any means.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Delve Infernal Records</strong> ◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You cite your contract's discovery of evidence clause. The contract casts Hypercognition.</p>","contracts/limitless-power":"<p>Each of these <em>bargained contracts</em> is unique, matching the contracted's idea of unlimited power. When you gain this contract, select one weapon in your possession, a common divine cantrip, and one common divine spell of each spell rank except 10th. The weapon becomes a +4 greater striking weapon. Once per day, from any distance, when you Activate this contract or Strike with the selected weapon, the devil who holds your bargained contract can call upon their divine right as a free action to have the spell or Strike target you or have its area centered on you instead of its intended targets.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate—Unholy Demand</strong> ◆◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per week</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You call upon a right of self-determination article in your contract. The contract casts manifestation (spell attack modifier +30, DC 40). Your contractor is immediately made aware of which spell you are duplicating.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate—Unleash Power</strong> ◆ to ◆◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The contract casts one of the selected spells (spell attack modifier +30, DC 40). The contract can cast each non-cantrip spell only once per day. You use the same number of actions for this activation as the selected spell normally takes.</p><hr><p><strong>Destruction</strong> The contract bursts into flame if the devil who signed it is slain and a celestial of equal or higher level declares it void.</p>","contracts/pits-protection":"<p>You are protected from physical harm. You gain resistance 5 to non-magical physical damage (except silver). Once per day, at any distance, the devil who holds this bargained contract can invoke a punitive damages clause as a single action with the concentrate trait to deal fire damage to you equal to twice your level, ignoring resistances, and gain half that many Hit Points.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Reasonable Force</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You cite a right of self-defense article in your contract. The contract casts Diabolical Mantle, and you can then Shove or Demoralize an adjacent creature.</p>","contracts/unholy-skill":"<p>Whether because of a lack of talent or a desire for fame, you've bargained for infernal aid. When you gain this contract, choose a skill. You gain a +2 item bonus to checks with that skill. Once per week, at any distance, the devil who holds your bargained contract can cite a royalties clause, taking from you the amount of currency you'd gain from Earning Income on an expert-rank task of your level. The currency teleports directly from your possessions to the devil's vaults. If you're unable to pay, the devil instead takes the item with a value higher than, but closest to, the amount you owe from your possessions as collateral, returning it when you pay the required amount.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Devil's Work</strong> ◆ (concentrate, magical, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You call upon your contract's apprenticeship clause. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your next skill action, and it gains the unholy trait.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-agate-ellipsoid":"<p>This aeon stone allows you to cast 2nd-rank Augury as a divine innate spell once per day.</p>\n<p>The resonant power causes the <em>augury</em> spell from the aeon stone to always succeed at the DC 6 Flat to give an answer other than \"nothing.\"</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-amber-sphere":"<p>If you are undead, your body regains much of the appearance it had in life, and you gain a +2 item bonus to Deception to Impersonate yourself as a living creature. If you're alive, your appearance is the healthiest version of yourself, and you gain a +2 item bonus to Make an Impression or Request that involves your strength or vigor.</p>\n<p>The resonant power of the <em>amber sphere</em> grants you a special activation to improve your salubrious appearance to a lurid extreme.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆◆ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The stone casts a 7th-rank Mask of Terror on you (DC 34 Will), causing your appearance to burst with a profusion of shocking vigor: your mouth fills with large and bright teeth, your hair animates in grasping tresses, your face flushes with bright blood that seeps from your skin, or similar. The image is unique to each observer, but you remain recognizably yourself regardless of the illusion's form.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-amplifying":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>An <em>Amplifying aeon stone</em> must be activated to provide a benefit. The resonant power grants you a +2 item bonus to Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion checks-whichever corresponds to the tradition of the last spell you enhanced with this <em>aeon stone</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate—Amplify</strong> ◆ (concentrate, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a Spell, that spell's rank is 1 higher (maximum 10th rank) for the purposes of counteracting and being counteracted.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone Resonance (Amplifying)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-azure-briolette":"<p>This aeon stone must be activated to provide a benefit.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ⤾ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy fails its save against a mental spell you cast using one of your spell slots</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice the spell's rank until your next turn.</p>\n<p>The resonant power grants a separate activation.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆◆ command, Interact</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain the effect of a Void Warp arcane cantrip.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-black-disc":"<p>This aeon stone slowly infuses void energy into your body. The stone deals 1 persistent void damage to you (10 void damage per minute) so long as it's invested, and you can't recover from persistent void damage while you have the stone invested.</p>\n<p>The resonant power grants you resistance 10 to holy and to vitality damage.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone Resonance (Black Disc)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-black-pearl":"<p>This black pearl sparkles with light. The resonant power allows you to cast Sending once per day.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ⤾ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> you are targeted by a mental effect</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You receive a +4 status bonus to your saving throw against the triggering effect.</p>\n<p>Whether or not your save is successful, the aeon stone attempts a counteract check at 1d20+30 to immediately reflect a copy of the effect back at the originator, targeting it using the creature's own relevant statistics but controlling the effect as if you had cast it.</p>\n<p>Every time you activate this aeon stone, attempt a DC 5 Flat. On a failure, the stone shatters and loses its magical properties forever.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone (Black Pearl)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-clear-quartz-octagon":"<p>This clear quartz stone appears to have been smashed and then repaired by pouring molten copper into the cracks and fitting the shards back together using the copper as a sort of mortar. When a non-magical item in your possession with a value of 90 gp or less and a Bulk of 1 Bulk or less would become broken, this aeon stone automatically activates, preventing the item from breaking by restoring the item's current Hit Points to the item's maximum Hit Points. The stone then turns permanently into a <em>Aeon Stone (Dull Grey)</em>.</p>\n<p>The stone's resonant power allows you to cast 1st-rank Mending as a divine innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-consumed":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>A <em>consumed</em> aeon stone is a dull lump that has lost its magical properties. It still rotates your head like any other aeon stone and can thus serve as a stylish, hand-free option for various spells that target an object.</p>\n<p>This aeon stone has no resonant power.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-crescent":"<p>Aeon stones are magical, intricately cut gemstones that orbit the head of their owners and grant them a magical effect. The ancient Azlanti empire made many advances in aeon stone technology, creating countless new aeon stones and devising innovative methods to use aeon stones to their greatest effect. The first wayfinders—one of many devices in which aeon stones can be slotted to gain additional resonant powers—were created in Azlant.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an aeon stone with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of aeon stones, each with a different appearance, magical effect, and resonant power.</p><hr><p>Once holy relics, the creation of <em>crescent aeon stones</em> was inspired by Acavna, goddess of the moon and protection. The <em>crescent aeon stone</em> continually sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Moonbeam</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, divine, holy, light, spirit)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The <em>crescent aeon stone</em> fires a blast of silvery moonlight in a 100-foot line, dealing 4d12 spirit damage to all creatures in the area (DC 22 basic Reflex save). This is silver damage for the purposes of weaknesses, resistances, and the like.</p>\n<p>The resonant power enables you to cast Forbidding Ward as a divine innate cantrip.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-cymophane-cabochon":"<p>Jabalis use the <em>cymophane cabochon aeon stone</em> to keep an eye on their belongings and surroundings. You gain a +2 item bonus to Perception checks and DCs against Hide, Sneak, and Steal actions.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast See the Unseen as an arcane innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-delaying":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>When you would die from the Dying condition (typically at dying 4), this smooth pink stone automatically activates and reduces your dying value to 1 less than would normally kill you (typically to dying 3). The stone then permanently turns into a Aeon Stone (Consumed). You can benefit from this ability only once per day, even if you have multiple such stones.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast 1st-rank Heal as a divine innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-dusty-rose-prism":"<p>This aeon stone allows you to cast the 1st-rank Shield cantrip as an arcane innate spell, surrounding yourself in pink energy.</p>\n<p>The resonant power increases the damage prevented by your aeon stone's shield spell from 5 to 10.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-eastern-star":"<p>This red crystal is cut in the shape of a five-pointed star. An eastern star aeon stone must be activated to provide a benefit. The resonant power grants you a +1 item bonus to Diplomacy checks.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Absorb Language</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You touch a creature who spoke a common language in your presence within the previous minute. The eastern star aeon stone becomes infused with this language, granting you the ability to understand, speak, and write that language. This activation persists until you activate it again.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-envisioning":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>This clear cube allows you to communicate with a limited form of telepathy to a range of 100 feet. The messages are transmitted as a simple image each round. These images are the quality of a hasty or childish sketch but can be roughly understood by creatures regardless of language. This provides no special ability to respond to your images.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Translate as an occult innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-flickering":"<p>Aeon stones are magical, intricately cut gemstones that orbit the head of their owners and grant them a magical effect. The ancient Azlanti empire made many advances in aeon stone technology, creating countless new aeon stones and devising innovative methods to use aeon stones to their greatest effect. The first wayfinders—one of many devices in which aeon stones can be slotted to gain additional resonant powers—were created in Azlant.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an aeon stone with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of aeon stones, each with a different appearance, magical effect, and resonant power.</p><hr><p>A flickering aeon stone contains a drop of orichalcum at its center. It remains slightly out of phase with reality, giving it a translucent appearance.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Flicker</strong> ◆</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The flickering aeon stone draws you slightly out of sync with the flow of time, causing you to flicker in and out of existence. You become Concealed for 1 minute, but you can't use this concealment to Hide or Sneak.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Enter Stasis</strong> ◆</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The flickering aeon stone pulls you from the flow of time completely, placing you in temporary stasis while you heal, then returning you to reality at the moment you left. You regain 2d10+8 healing Hit Points. If you have the clumsy, drained, enfeebled, or stupefied condition, the value of each of these conditions is reduced by 1.</p>\n<p>The resonant power grants you a +1 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-formulating":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p><hr><p>This four-sided prism is imbued with knowledge for the construction of several objects. The stone contains the knowledge of all formulas found in a basic crafter's book. While you have the stone invested, you have the full knowledge of the stone's formulas. This counts as having the formula for the purposes of Crafting checks. While you have this knowledge, you can write the formulas down for later use, such as if you lose access to the stone. You also gain a +1 item bonus to skill checks made to Craft while the stone is invested.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Phantasmal Minion as an arcane innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-gold-nodule":"<p>When a gold nodule aeon stone is created, its creator chooses a language they know to store within the crystal. When you invest the stone, you gain the ability to understand, speak, and write that language.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Translate as an occult innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-lavender-and-green-ellipsoid":"<p>This functions as a pale lavender ellipsoid aeon stone, but it casts an 8th-rank Dispel Magic spell with a counteract modifier of 1d20+31.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Detect Magic and Read Aura as arcane innate spells at will.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-mottled-ellipsoid":"<p>This aeon stone alters your life force. You gain void healing, which means you are damaged by vitality energy and not healed by vitality healing effects. You don't take void damage, and you are healed by void effects that heal undead.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast 7th-rank False Vitality once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-nourishing":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>After you've invested and worn this transparent stone for a week continuously, you no longer need to eat or drink. This time resets if you remove the <em>aeon stone</em> or it's invested by someone else.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Air Bubble as a primal innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-olivine-pendeloque":"<p>An <em>olivine pendeloque aeon stone</em> imparts the calmness of still earth and a solidity of thought, granting you a +3 item bonus to saving throws against effects that cause the Confused, Frightened, or Stupefied conditions.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Still Earth</strong> ⤾ (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You become confused, frightened, or stupefied</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The stone suppresses the triggering effect for 1 minute, but the calming urges impose a –1 status penalty to your attack rolls.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-pale-lavender-ellipsoid":"<p>This aeon stone must be activated to provide a benefit. The resonant power allows you to cast the Read Aura cantrip as an arcane innate spell.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ⤾ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A spell targets you</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The stone casts a 6th-rank Dispel Magic spell in an attempt to counteract the triggering spell, with a counteract modifier of 1d20+22. This can be used only on spells that specifically target you-not area spells that don't have targets. If it succeeds, it counteracts the spell for all targets if other creatures were targeted in addition to you.</p>\n<p>Each time you activate this <em>aeon stone</em>, attempt a DC 5 Flat. On a failure, the stone permanently turns into a <em>dull gray aeon stone</em>.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-pale-orange-rhomboid":"<p>The first time each day you die, your vital and spiritual essences mingle together and reside within this aeon stone.</p>\n<p>You have a limited sense of how many life forces are currently within 30 feet of the stone, which you can potentially use to determine when it's safe to call on the stone's power. At any time within the next hour after your body died, you can spend 1 minute concentrating in order to return to your body.</p>\n<p>As long as your body is still intact, you are no longer dead- you are restored to 1 HP with the Doomed 3 and Wounded 3 conditions. You can benefit from the effects of only one pale orange rhomboid aeon stone in a given day.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to wait more than an hour to return to your body with the aeon stone; as long as the wayfinder remains on the body, your body doesn't decay and you can return at any point.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-pearlescent-pyramid":"<p>While invested, this <em>aeon stone</em> grants the benefit of the <em>Ghost Touch</em> property rune to your weapons and unarmed attacks.</p>\n<p>The resonant power grants a special activation.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain the effects of See the Unseen for 1 round.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-pearly-white-spindle":"<p>When you invest this <em>aeon stone</em>, it slowly starts healing your wounds, restoring 1 HP every minute.</p>\n<p>The resonant power grants you resistance 1 to void damage.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone Resonance (Pearly White Spindle)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-peering":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>This faintly colored prism catches and transforms light. If the aeon stone is in an area of bright light, shades of purple light provide dim light in a 30-foot radius. In that radius, magical items and effects are tinged with purple, the depth of the color revealing their counteract rank.</p>\n<p>The GM also secretly rolls a counteract check against any darkness or illusion effect the light touches. It has a counteract modifier of +25. If the light fails to counteract an effect, it won't try again for 24 hours.</p>\n<p>Inside a <em>wayfinder</em>, the <em>aeon stone</em> cannot catch light. However, its resonant power lets you activate or deactivate the <em>aeon stone's</em> light emitting from the <em>wayfinder</em> as an Interact action.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-pink-rhomboid":"<p>When you invest this stone, you gain 15 temporary Hit Points. If the stone's effects are suppressed, you lose any of the temporary Hit Points remaining until it returns. The temporary Hit Points refresh during your daily preparations; they do not refresh if you re-invest the stone, or invest another <em>pink rhomboid aeon stone</em>, before then.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast the Stabilize cantrip as a divine innate spell.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone (Pink Rhomboid)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-polished-pebble":"<p>A <em>polished pebble aeon stone</em> imbues you with the strength of the earth, granting a +1 item bonus to saves and DCs against attempts to grapple or swallow you.</p>\n<p>The stone's resonant power allows you to cast Grease as a primal innate spell once per day. You can target only surfaces, not objects, with this spell.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-preserving":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>This red crystalline star covers you in a faint aura when you are subject to lingering wounds. You gain resistance 3 to persistent damage. At the end of any turn where the persistent damage can't overcome this resistance, end that condition.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Stabilize as a primal innate cantrip.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-rainbow-prism":"<p>While this aeon stone orbits your head, the flat part of its base tumbles to briefly face creatures you can see within 30 feet, as though the stone is watching them. You can activate this stone in two ways.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆◆ envision</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The aeon stone captures the image of a creature of your size that you can see within 30 feet. It can have up to 3 images captured at a time; if you capture a fourth, you decide which image it replaces.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆◆ envision</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> three times per day</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The prism is storing at least one image of a creature of your size</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The aeon stone casts a 3rd-rank Illusory Disguise on you, which must be of one of the creatures it has currently captured. While you are under the effects of this spell, the aeon stone is Invisible.</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows the stone to capture up to 5 images. If removed from the <em>wayfinder</em>, you must decide which images to lose.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-repairing":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p><hr><p>This translucent, spherical stone's center contains a multitude of sparkling, colored flecks. While you have this stone invested, you gain a +1 item bonus to skill checks made to Craft. Additionally, when Repairing an item, you restore an additional 5 Hit Points to the item (10 Hit Points on a critical success).</p>\n<p>The resonant power allows you to cast Mending as an arcane innate spell once per day.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-smoothing":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>This spherical piece of silvery stone helps you ignore minor issues. You can ignore status penalties to skill checks from Clumsy 1, Enfeebled 1, Frightened 1, Sickened 1, and Stupefied 1 conditions as long as the value of that condition is 1.</p>\n<p>Its resonant power allows you to cast Guidance as an occult innate cantrip.</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-sprouting":"<p>Over millennia, these mysterious, intricately cut gemstones have been hoarded by mystics and fanatics hoping to discover their secrets. Despite their myriad forms and functions, these stones are purportedly all fragments of crystal tools used by otherworldly entities to construct the universe in primeval times.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an <em>aeon stone</em> with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of <em>aeon stones</em>, each with a different appearance and magical effect. Each <em>aeon stone</em> also gains a resonant power when slotted into a special magical item called a <em>wayfinder</em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Encouraging the natural growth of life, this green ovoid can often be found surrounded by new seedlings. Its resonant power allows you to cast Tangle Vine as a primal innate cantrip.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Activate—Flow of Life</strong> ⤾ (concentrate, vitality)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You are healed by a vitality effect or took void damage</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain 8 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone (Sprouting)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-vital-amplification":"<p>Aeon stones are magical, intricately cut gemstones that orbit the head of their owners and grant them a magical effect. The ancient Azlanti empire made many advances in aeon stone technology, creating countless new aeon stones and devising innovative methods to use aeon stones to their greatest effect. The first wayfinders—one of many devices in which aeon stones can be slotted to gain additional resonant powers—were created in Azlant.</p>\n<p>When you invest one of these precisely shaped crystals, the stone orbits your head instead of being worn on your body. You can stow an aeon stone with an Interact action, and an orbiting stone can be snatched out of the air with a successful Disarm action against you. A stowed or removed stone remains invested, but its effects are suppressed until you return it to orbit your head again.</p>\n<p>There are various types of aeon stones, each with a different appearance, magical effect, and resonant power.</p><hr><p>A vital amplification aeon stone improves the flow of vital energy through your body, speeding the healing process and safeguarding your body from life-draining effects. Whenever you regain Hit Points, you regain an additional 1 Hit Point for each 10 Hit Points regained (minimum 1 additional Hit Point). The resonant power grants you resistance 5 to void damage.</p>\n<p>Effect: Aeon Stone Resonance (Vital Amplification)</p>","aeon-stones/aeon-stone-western-star":"<p>This blue crystal is cut in the shape of a five-pointed star. A western star aeon stone must be activated to provide a benefit. The resonant power grants you a +1 item bonus to Deception checks.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Illusory Disguise</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, illusion, manipulate, visual)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The western star aeon stone casts a 1st-rank Illusory Disguise to your specifications. If you so choose, the disguise obscures any aeon stones orbiting your head, rendering them invisible until the activation ends.</p>","tattoos/arclord-eye":"<p>These tattoos take the form of an eye nestled within a triangle and are usually worn on the brow; their inks are said to be distilled from rare materials found only within the Crux of Nex. However, their popularity casts some doubt upon this claim. When you target a Concealed creature with a magical effect or spell, you reduce the DC of the flat check to 3.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Open the Eye</strong> ◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> For the next 10 minutes, you gain an imprecise magic sense with a range of 30 feet. This allows you to detect spells, magical effects, and magical items within range. You also learn the rank or level of such magical effects and their traits. Deceptive illusion magic is not detectable by this magic sense.</p>","tattoos/calamitys-bane-tattoo":"<p>This small tattoo of a stylized lidded or clouded eye radiating lines of power is inked on a part of your body that you cannot easily see with your own eyes, such as the nape of your neck, behind your ears, or your interscapular region. This tattoo protects you during calamity as well as uncertainty, guiding your intuition to take subconscious actions and precautions to shelter you in a thousand unknown ways. When you are affected by a misfortune effect or a curse, your shrouded eye tattoo emits an intense sensation akin to pins and needles, alerting you that something is awry, though the specific nature of the danger might be unknown to you.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Alleviate Uncertainty</strong> ◇ (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per 10 minutes</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You make a check for an action that has the secret trait or that has been affected by a misfortune effect</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You gain a +1 status bonus to the check associated with the triggering action.</p>","tattoos/chiromantic-lines":"<p>These tattoos boast minute, intricate inscriptions, inked with dust ground from the eyelashes of omen dragons. The process is incredibly painful, involving tattooing one's pupils as well as one's palm lines with an almost invisible series of tracings.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Cunning Consultation</strong> ◆ (concentrate, prediction)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> This tattoo becomes temporarily visible, allowing you to briefly grasp the very near future just enough to predict the subtle movements of those around you. Until the end of the turn, all creatures you can see that are not Concealed or hidden are Off-Guard to you.</p>","tattoos/dreamers-butterfly":"<p>These twin tattoos, each depicting the ornate wing of a butterfly or moth, are usually placed upon your palms or wrists. While sleeping, this tattoo crafts lucid dreams that don't disturb your rest; However, when danger arises, these dreams shift to alert you to trouble and shroud you in camouflaging dream-stuff. As a result, you do not take any penalty to Perception checks when asleep. When asleep, you also gain a +2 circumstance to your Will saves against effects with the dream or sleep traits.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Wake the Dream</strong> ◆ (illusion, manipulate, mental)</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> By touching the two halves of the tattoo together, the wings expand to show a small illusory rendition of any effects with the dream or sleep traits you are currently subject to. Onlookers (including yourself) gain a +1 status bonus to checks to Identify Magic of any spells or magical effects with the dream or sleep traits for 1 round.</p><hr><p><strong>Special</strong> An adjacent ally can also Activate this effect by touching the two halves of your tattoo together if you are willing or Unconscious.</p>","tattoos/golden-souled-yang-na":"<p><strong>Prerequisites</strong> worshipper of a deity or pantheon</p><hr><p>The traditions of these large tattoos, often stretching over the back or shoulders, have been passed from Tang Mai's tree-keeping priests to their students across Tian Xia.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Soul Blessing</strong> ◇ (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You take an action with the rage, stance, or tandem trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The tattoo purifies your mind and body, reducing your clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, or stupefied condition by 1.</p><hr><p><strong>Special</strong> While you are under the effect of Rage, the Soul Blessing action gains the rage trait.</p>","tattoos/nine-void-sleeves":"<p>The ink on these tattoos, made from the crushed crystalline fangs and wingbones of sceaduinars, lends a dull purple-black hue to your arms and hands. During combat, the ink moves of its own accord, coalescing into nine smoky crystal spurs of darkness; these eerie finger-like protrusions move with an unearthly grace on your command, supplying the requisite magical gestures for your spells.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Shadow Fingers</strong> ◆ (concentrate, shadow, spellshape)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per 10 minutes</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If your next action is to Cast a Spell with the void trait, your spell loses the manipulate trait and gains the shadow trait, as the tattoo's shadowy spurs perform the gestures in your stead.</p>","intelligent-weapons/meloths-lifedrinker-level-7":"<p><strong>Perception</strong> +11; precise darkvision 40 feet, imprecise hearing 30 feet</p>\n<p><strong>Communication</strong> telepathy (Azlanti, Chthonian, Common)</p>\n<p><strong>Skills</strong> Deception +13, Intimidation +11, Occultism +10, Religion +11</p>\n<p><strong>Int</strong> +2, <strong>Wis</strong> +3, <strong>Cha</strong> +5</p>\n<p><strong>Will</strong> +11</p><hr><p><em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> is a +1 longsword whose blade appears to be made of obsidian pitted with pocks and scars that, upon closer examination, are tiny images of screaming faces, their haunted visages twisted in pain and fear. It was once a much more powerful weapon, until Sarnax used it as a prison to contain the essence of its original wielder—a demon lord named Meloth. The magic that once granted the blade its power immediately transformed and refocused into the task of serving as a prison for the demon lord, leaving the sword a shadow of its prior glory and infusing it with an unnatural weight three times that of a typical longsword. Over the centuries, Meloth has become able to observe and manipulate the world around the blade</p>\n<p>Meloth's ability to influence the world around him via illusions is limited to those events detailed in the adventure, but a PC who ends up carrying the cursed sword for an extended length of time (beyond the scope of this adventure) might find similar illusions manifesting to further torment them, their companions, and anyone around them. Even then, Meloth won't directly communicate with his wielder unless he's fused to them.</p>\n<p>A character who holds Meloth's Lifedrinker must make a DC 18 Will save to resist Meloth's influence at the end of every round they continue to hold the weapon (one can safely—but awkwardly—transport Meloth's Lifedrinker by picking it up, moving, and then dropping it before ending oneʼs turn).</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The character is temporarily immune to Meloth's influence for 24 hours and can carry or wield the sword normally as a +1 longsword.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The character is unaffected by Meloth's influence this round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> Meloth's Lifedrinker fuses with the character. As part of this bond, Meloth absorbs some of the character's life, reducing the character's maximum HP by 6 (to a minimum of 1) for as long as the character remains fused to the sword. Meloth now communicates with the fused character via telepathy—encouraging them through lies, coercion, and threats to commit more and more atrocities while seeking a way to somehow free him from this prison.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but it reduces the character's maximum HP by 12 (to a minimum of 1).</p><hr><p>If during the first interlude of the Test of Aroden a PC allows Meloth to awaken the blade, the result empowers <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> into a <em>+1 striking wounding longsword</em>. As long as a character carries Meloth's Lifedrinker, they can speak and understand Chthonian. In addition, this empowered version of the blade gains the following activations.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate—Lifedrink</strong> ⤾ (death, divine, void)</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> scores a critical hit on a living creature with a level equal to or higher than its wielder</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> inflicts 1d6 additional void damage to the living creature. If the creature struck by the critical hit is slain by its damage, the blade impales its victim. Black, oily energy like wet smoke pours from the victim's eyes and flows to the ebon sword, desiccating the corpse in an instant as all of its liquid seeps into the Lifedrinker, leaving the body a dried-out husk.</p>\n<p>The first time this happens when its wielder is at least 10th level, <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker's +1 weapon potency</em> rune permanently becomes a <em>+2 weapon potency</em> rune. The first time this happens when its wielder is at least 12th level, <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker's</em> striking rune permanently becomes a greater striking rune. The first time this happens when its wielder is at least 16th level, <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker's</em> <em>+2 weapon potency</em> rune permanently becomes a <em>+3 weapon potency</em> rune. And the first time this happens when its wielder is at least 19th level, <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker's</em> <em>greater striking</em> rune permanently becomes a <em>major striking rune</em>.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate—Vision of Meloth</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, death, emotion, fear, mental)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> causes a creature within 60 feet to experience a harrowing vision in which Meloth, as he appeared in life (a vaguely humanoid horned demon not quite bat nor leech nor blood-drinking fly), leaps from the blade to surge forward and devour the target. The wielder of <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> sees this as well, but no other observers do. The targeted creature takes 6d6 mental damage with a Will save; the DC is equal to the wielder's class or spell DC, whichever is higher. If the target is reduced to 0 HP by this effect, the vision becomes reality and kills the target instantly. Onlookers see only the target swiftly and gorily consumed by unseen mouths over the course of a few seconds, after which a mutilated carcass drops to the ground, lifeless. As an intelligent weapon, <em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> can activate this ability on a whim, and often does so when the sword senses a creature that would be likely to die as a result of this activation—be that creature friend or foe of the wielder.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage and is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage and is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage, is Frightened 4, and is Slowed 1 as long as it remains frightened.</p>","intelligent-weapons/meloths-lifedrinker":"<p><strong>Perception</strong> +11; precise darkvision 40 feet, imprecise hearing 30 feet</p>\n<p><strong>Communication</strong> telepathy (Azlanti, Chthonian, Common)</p>\n<p><strong>Skills</strong> Deception +13, Intimidation +11, Occultism +10, Religion +11</p>\n<p><strong>Int</strong> +2, <strong>Wis</strong> +3, <strong>Cha</strong> +5</p>\n<p><strong>Will</strong> +11</p><hr><p><em>Meloth's Lifedrinker</em> is a +1 longsword whose blade appears to be made of obsidian pitted with pocks and scars that, upon closer examination, are tiny images of screaming faces, their haunted visages twisted in pain and fear. It was once a much more powerful weapon, until Sarnax used it as a prison to contain the essence of its original wielder—a demon lord named Meloth. The magic that once granted the blade its power immediately transformed and refocused into the task of serving as a prison for the demon lord, leaving the sword a shadow of its prior glory and infusing it with an unnatural weight three times that of a typical longsword. Over the centuries, Meloth has become able to observe and manipulate the world around the blade</p>\n<p>Meloth's ability to influence the world around him via illusions is limited to those events detailed in the adventure, but a PC who ends up carrying the cursed sword for an extended length of time (beyond the scope of this adventure) might find similar illusions manifesting to further torment them, their companions, and anyone around them. Even then, Meloth won't directly communicate with his wielder unless he's fused to them.</p>\n<p>A character who holds Meloth's Lifedrinker must make a DC 18 Will save to resist Meloth's influence at the end of every round they continue to hold the weapon (one can safely—but awkwardly—transport Meloth's Lifedrinker by picking it up, moving, and then dropping it before ending oneʼs turn).</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The character is temporarily immune to Meloth's influence for 24 hours and can carry or wield the sword normally as a +1 longsword.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The character is unaffected by Meloth's influence this round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> Meloth's Lifedrinker fuses with the character. As part of this bond, Meloth absorbs some of the character's life, reducing the character's maximum HP by 6 (to a minimum of 1) for as long as the character remains fused to the sword. Meloth now communicates with the fused character via telepathy—encouraging them through lies, coercion, and threats to commit more and more atrocities while seeking a way to somehow free him from this prison.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but it reduces the character's maximum HP by 12 (to a minimum of 1).</p>","spellhearts/all-seeing-eye-greater":"<p>This glass eyeball is slightly uncanny due to the two brightly colored crystal irises it sports on opposing sides. It helps combatants see their foes even in the darkest of situations. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 20.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 4 to damage from illusion effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> (fortune) After you cast a light spell by Activating the eye, your own eyesight sharpens until the end of your next turn. If you fail the flat check to target a Concealed or hidden opponent with a Strike with the weapon, you can reroll it and take the new result.</p></li></ul><p>DC 20 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Light.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Revealing Light.</p>","spellhearts/all-seeing-eye":"<p>This glass eyeball is slightly uncanny due to the two brightly colored crystal irises it sports on opposing sides. It helps combatants see their foes even in the darkest of situations.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 2 to damage from illusion effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> (fortune) After you cast a light spell by Activating the eye, your own eyesight sharpens until the end of your next turn. If you fail the flat check to target a Concealed or Hidden opponent with a Strike with the weapon, you can reroll it and take the new result.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Light.</p>","spellhearts/cerebral-barbell-greater":"<p>This tiny metallic barbell is strangely heavy for its size. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +14 and the DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 24.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 2 to force.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After casting a spell by Activating the cerebral barbell, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 3 force damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 24 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Projectile.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Iron Rain.</p>","spellhearts/cerebral-barbell-major":"<p>This tiny metallic barbell is strangely heavy for its size. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +19 and the DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 29.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 2 to force.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After casting a spell by Activating the cerebral barbell, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 4 force damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 29 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Projectile.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast a 4th-rank Iron Rain.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Magnetize.</p>","spellhearts/cerebral-barbell":"<p>This tiny metallic barbell is strangely heavy for its size. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +7.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 2 to force.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After casting a spell by Activating the cerebral barbell, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 2 force damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cerebral Barbell - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Projectile.</p>","spellhearts/cheery-chime-greater":"<p>This single crystalline wind chime occasionally jingles as if blown against another chime by a soothing breeze. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating the item is 24.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws against emotion effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast an emotion spell by Activating the cheery chime, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d6 mental damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 24 basic Will</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Infectious Enthusiasm</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Laughing Fit</p>","spellhearts/cheery-chime-major":"<p>This single crystalline wind chime occasionally jingles as if blown against another chime by a soothing breeze. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating the item is 34.</p><ul><li><p>Armor You gain a +3 item bonus to saving throws against emotion effects.</p></li><li><p>Weapon After you cast an emotion spell by Activating the cheery chime, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d8 mental damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 34 basic Will</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Infectious Enthusiasm</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Laughing Fit</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 6th-rank Roaring Applause</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Zealous Conviction</p>","spellhearts/cheery-chime":"<p>This single crystalline wind chime occasionally jingles as if blown against another chime by a soothing breeze.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws against emotion effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast an emotion spell by Activating the cheery chime, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d4 mental damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Cheery Chime - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Infectious Enthusiasm</p>","spellhearts/deathbane-crescent-greater":"<p>This crescent moon carved out of bone holds the power to turn back the undead. This spellheart covers any item it's affixed to with spiderwebs that reappear even if damaged or removed. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 24.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, you gain resistance 5 to attacks and effects from undead creatures until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d6 vitality damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Deathbane Crescent - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 24 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Vitality Lash.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 3rd-rank Infuse Vitality.</p>","spellhearts/deathbane-crescent-major":"<p>This crescent moon carved out of bone holds the power to turn back the undead. This spellheart covers any item it's affixed to with spiderwebs that reappear even if damaged or removed. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 30.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, you gain resistance 10 to attacks and effects from undead creatures until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d8 vitality damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Deathbane Crescent - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 30 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Vitality Lash.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 3rd-rank Infuse Vitality.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> you cast 4th-rank Sound Body.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Vital Beacon.</p>","spellhearts/deathbane-crescent":"<p>This crescent moon carved out of bone holds the power to turn back the undead. This spellheart covers any item it's affixed to with spiderwebs that reappear even if damaged or removed. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 18.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, you gain resistance 2 to attacks and effects from undead creatures until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a vitality spell by Activating the crescent, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1d4 vitality damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Deathbane Crescent - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 18 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Vitality Lash.</p>","spellhearts/energizing-vial-greater":"<p>This sealed glass vial has no stopper and is filled with pure white light. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +21 and the spell DC is 31.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, you can Step as a free action once per round until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d6 persistent electricity damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Energizing Vial - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 31 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Live Wire</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 5th-rank lightning lasso</p>","spellhearts/energizing-vial-major":"<p>This sealed glass vial has no stopper and is filled with pure white light. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +28 and spell DC is 38.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, you can Step as a free action once per round until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d8 persistent electricity damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Energizing Vial - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 38 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Live Wire</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 8th-rank Lightning Lasso</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 8th-rank Draw the Lightning</p>","spellhearts/energizing-vial":"<p>This sealed glass vial has no stopper and is filled with pure white light. The spell attack modifier of any spell cast by Activating this item is +13.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, you can Step as a free action once per round until the end of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast an electricity spell by Activating the energizing vial, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d4 persistent electricity damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Energizing Vial - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Live Wire</p>","spellhearts/helping-hand-greater":"<p>This miniature wooden hand has fully articulated fingers with brass joints. The tiny hand twitches infrequently of its own accord, especially if scrutinized for too long.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limit by 2.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> You gain a +2 item bonus to skill checks to Aid when wielding the weapon.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Helping Hand - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Helping Hand - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Hand.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 3rd-rank Mending.</p>","spellhearts/helping-hand-major":"<p>This miniature wooden hand has fully articulated fingers with brass joints. The tiny hand twitches infrequently of its own accord, especially if scrutinized for too long.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limit by 3.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> You gain a +2 item bonus to skill checks to Aid when wielding the weapon.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Helping Hand - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Helping Hand - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Hand.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 3rd-rank Mending.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Imaginary Lockbox.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Haul.</p>","spellhearts/helping-hand":"<p>This miniature wooden hand has fully articulated fingers with brass joints. The tiny hand twitches infrequently of its own accord, especially if scrutinized for too long.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limit by 1.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> You gain a +1 item bonus to skill checks to Aid when wielding the weapon.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Helping Hand - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Helping Hand - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Telekinetic Hand.</p>","spellhearts/hydrating-pinwheel-greater":"<p>Clear streams of water have been magically solidified into a glimmering, iridescent pinwheel that looks as fragile as glass. When affixed, it spins gently without a breeze. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 31.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 3 to persistent acid damage and persistent fire damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a water spell by Activating the <em>enduring helix</em>, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d6 persistent cold damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 31 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Rousing Splash.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Geyser</p>","spellhearts/hydrating-pinwheel-major":"<p>Clear streams of water have been magically solidified into a glimmering, iridescent pinwheel that looks as fragile as glass. When affixed, it spins gently without a breeze. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 38.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 3 to persistent acid damage and persistent fire damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a water spell by Activating the <em>enduring helix</em>, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d8 persistent cold damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 38 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Rousing Splash.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 8th-rank Geyser</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 8th-rank Soothing Spring</p>","spellhearts/hydrating-pinwheel":"<p>Clear streams of water have been magically solidified into a glimmering, iridescent pinwheel that looks as fragile as glass. When affixed, it spins gently without a breeze.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain resistance 3 to persistent acid damage and persistent fire damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a water spell by Activating the <em>enduring helix</em>, your Strikes with the weapon deal 1d4 persistent cold damage until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Hydrating Pinwheel - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Rousing Splash.</p>","spellhearts/silver-tongue-greater":"<p>This tongue-shaped silver trinket typically dangles from a silver chain. It seems to catch the light wherever it is affixed. When affixed to armor or a weapon with any metal components, it makes those pieces gleam brightly. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 34.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain a +3 item bonus to saving throws against auditory and linguistic effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a mental spell by Activating the silver tongue, you gain a +3 item bonus to Intimidation checks to Demoralize until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Silver Tongue - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Silver Tongue - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 34 basic Will</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Daze.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> you cast 6th-rank Biting Words.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> you cast 6th-rank Charm.</p>","spellhearts/silver-tongue":"<p>This tongue-shaped silver trinket typically dangles from a silver chain. It seems to catch the light wherever it is affixed. When affixed to armor or a weapon with any metal components, it makes those pieces gleam brightly. The spell DC of any spell cast by Activating this item is 24.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> You gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws against auditory and linguistic effects.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> After you cast a mental spell by Activating the silver tongue, you gain a +2 item bonus to Intimidation checks to Demoralize until the end of your next turn.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Silver Tongue - Armor</p>\n<p>Effect: Silver Tongue - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 24 basic Will</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Daze.</p>","spellhearts/thirsty-chalice-greater":"<p>This slate chalice improbably holds one single drop of water in it at all times and helps refresh the wearer, sometimes at the expense of their enemies. The DC of all spells cast by Activating this item is 22.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, you are surrounded by a fine mist. You become Concealed until the beginning of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> (void) After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 2 void damage until the end of your next turn; the first time in a round you successfully deal this void damage, you gain 8 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Thirsty Chalice - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 22 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Draw Moisture.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Curse of Lost Time.</p>","spellhearts/thirsty-chalice-major":"<p>This slate chalice improbably holds one single drop of water in it at all times and helps refresh the wearer, sometimes at the expense of their enemies. The DC of all spells cast by Activating this item is 35.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, you are surrounded by a fine mist. You become Concealed until the beginning of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> (void) After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 4 void damage until the end of your next turn; the first time in a round you successfully deal this void damage, you gain 16 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Thirsty Chalice - Weapon</p>\n<p>DC 35 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Draw Moisture.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 6th rank Curse of Lost Time.</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast 6th rank Vital Seed.</p>","spellhearts/thirsty-chalice":"<p>This slate chalice improbably holds one single drop of water in it at all times and helps refresh the wearer, sometimes at the expense of their enemies.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Armor</strong> After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, you are surrounded by a fine mist. You become Concealed until the beginning of your next turn.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon</strong> (void) After you cast a spell by Activating the chalice, your Strikes with the weapon deal an additional 1 void damage until the end of your next turn; the first time in a round you successfully deal this void damage, you gain 4 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.</p></li></ul><p>Effect: Thirsty Chalice - Weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Activate</strong> Cast a Spell</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You cast Draw Moisture.</p>","artifacts/flame-of-the-radiant-spark":"<p><strong>Activate</strong> ◆ (manipulate) The ancient lost artifact known as the Radiant Spark could bestow its flames upon the wick of any candle, after which the electric-blue flame would burn eternally until it is activated or the candle itself is jostled enough to move it (see Destruction below).</p>\n<p>You activate a <em>flame of the Radiant Spark</em> either by using your fingers to extinguish the flame or by blowing it out, causing the crackling blue energy to leap into your body and then settle in one of your hands. The blue flame continues to burn harmlessly on your hand, shedding illumination equivalent to a candle, and it can be extinguished only by your death or by expending it through calling upon the flame's power to cast a 6th-rank raise dead to your specifications. You can hold only one flame of the Radiant Spark at a time—if you activate another flame before your current one is extinguished, the new flame replaces the previous one. The PCs can get a hint at how to use the flames of the Radiant Spark in Sarnax's Tomb by deduction, as well as by careful study of the Radiant Spark wall panel at area <strong>B8</strong>.</p><hr><p><strong>Destruction</strong> While the Radiant Spark itself is nearly as indestructible as any other artifact, these flames created by its power are fragile. A candle bearing a flame of the Radiant Spark can burn forever, but any attempt to move the candle (including any accidental toppling over caused by nearby events) causes the flame to gutter. The flame can still be claimed if someone extinguishes it with their fingers within a minute, otherwise the flame goes out. Curiously, wind and water cannot extinguish a flame of the Radiant Spark once it burns on a candle's wick unless the force of the wind or water causes the candle itself to topple or float away.</p>","artifacts/heart-of-sarnax":"<p>This fist-sized ruby would be close to priceless even if it weren't a magical artifact. So large and heavy for a ruby that most merchants would take it for a fake anyway, the Heart of Sarnax pulses like a heartbeat whenever the wielder speaks aloud the name \"Sarnax.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Two Hearts as One</strong> ◆◆ (concentrate, manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> You hold forth the Heart of Sarnax, targeting a living creature within 60 feet, then give the huge ruby a firm squeeze. The Heart of Sarnax begins pounding in your grip, like a heart racing in panic or exertion, and the targeted creature feels their own heart speed up to match. Choose one of the following effects to apply to the targeted creature.</p>\n<p><strong>Bestow Vim</strong> The target creature becomes Quickened, and it can use the extra action to Stride, Strike, or attempt an Athletics check that resolves as a single action. Any Strikes made during this action are not affected by the creature's current multiple attack penalty, and any Athletics checks made during this action gain a +2 item bonus. If the creature uses the action to Stride, it gains a +10-foot item bonus to its Speed. This effect lasts for 1 minute, after which the target creature becomes Fatigued for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Crush Heart</strong> (death) The target creature feels its heart pounding harder, and then suddenly feels it stop as its life essence is crushed. The creature takes 7d6 spirit damage and must attempt a DC 20 Fortitude save. A creature reduced to 0 HP by this damage is slain.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes no damage, but is Off-Guard until the end of its next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is off-guard until the end of its next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, is off-guard until the end of its next turn, and is Slowed 1 for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is Stunned 3. When it recovers from being stunned, it is Slowed 2 for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Destruction</strong> By transforming the Heart of Sarnax into a ruby version of Sarnax and then destroying the construct, the Heart of Sarnax shatters into valuable but non-magical fragments.</p>"});
